# Dragon Magazine Compendium - alternative class features (built by acf_build.py; the repository's ACF pattern).


###Block: Paladin alternative class features
Angel's Sight	KEY:Paladin ACF ~ Angel's Sight (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PaladinACF.PaladinDivineHealth	PRECLASS:1,Paladin=3	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Angel's Sight (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.407	DESC:Alternative class feature (paladin, 3rd level). You are blessed with the ability to see as celestials do: darkvision 60 feet and low-light vision (no additional bonus if you already have one of these senses). Replaces divine health.
Angel's Sight	KEY:ACF ~ Angel's Sight (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Paladin Class Feature	BONUS:VAR|DarkvisionRange|60|TYPE=Base	VISION:Low-Light Vision	SOURCEPAGE:p.407	DESC:You are blessed with the ability to see as celestials do: darkvision 60 feet and low-light vision (no additional bonus if you already have one of these senses). Replaces divine health.
Aura of Banishment	KEY:Paladin ACF ~ Aura of Banishment (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PaladinACF.PaladinRemoveDisease	PRECLASS:1,Paladin=6	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Aura of Banishment (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.409	DESC:Alternative class feature (paladin, 6th level). An aura of banishment surrounds you to a distance of 30 feet, felt and suffered only by evil outsiders: no evil outsider with fewer Hit Dice than your paladin level (%1) can be summoned into this area, nor can such creatures use summoning or teleporting effects there. You gain a +2 bonus on Intimidate checks against evil outsiders. Replaces remove disease.
Aura of Banishment	KEY:ACF ~ Aura of Banishment (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Paladin Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.409	DESC:An aura of banishment surrounds you to a distance of 30 feet, felt and suffered only by evil outsiders: no evil outsider with fewer Hit Dice than your paladin level (%1) can be summoned into this area, nor can such creatures use summoning or teleporting effects there. You gain a +2 bonus on Intimidate checks against evil outsiders. Replaces remove disease.|PaladinLVL
Aura of Sanctity	KEY:Paladin ACF ~ Aura of Sanctity (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PaladinACF.PaladinTurnUndead	PRECLASS:1,Paladin=4	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Aura of Sanctity (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.409	DESC:Alternative class feature (paladin, 4th level). A sacred ritual conducted with a group of archons has left you with otherworldly protection: you are immune to one chosen effect - compulsion effects (including possession), death effects or petrification - and allies within your aura of courage gain a +4 bonus on saves against it. Replaces turn undead.
Aura of Sanctity	KEY:ACF ~ Aura of Sanctity (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Paladin Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Paladin ACF Aura of Sanctity|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.409	DESC:A sacred ritual conducted with a group of archons has left you with otherworldly protection: you are immune to one chosen effect - compulsion effects (including possession), death effects or petrification - and allies within your aura of courage gain a +4 bonus on saves against it. Replaces turn undead.
Aura of Sanctity (Compulsion)	KEY:ACF ~ Aura of Sanctity (DMC) ~ Compulsion	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:PaladinACFAuraofSanctity.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.409	DESC:You are immune to compulsion effects (including possession); allies within your aura of courage gain a +4 bonus on saves against them.
Aura of Sanctity (Death Effects)	KEY:ACF ~ Aura of Sanctity (DMC) ~ Death Effects	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:PaladinACFAuraofSanctity.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.409	DESC:You are immune to death effects; allies within your aura of courage gain a +4 bonus on saves against them.
Aura of Sanctity (Petrification)	KEY:ACF ~ Aura of Sanctity (DMC) ~ Petrification	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:PaladinACFAuraofSanctity.SpecialQuality	SOURCEPAGE:p.409	DESC:You are immune to petrification; allies within your aura of courage gain a +4 bonus on saves against it.
Dead Levels (Righteous Cause)	KEY:Paladin ACF ~ Dead Levels (Righteous Cause) (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PaladinACF.PaladinDeadLevels	PRECLASS:1,Paladin=7	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Dead Levels (Righteous Cause) (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.416	DESC:Alternative class feature (paladin, 7th level). Optional rule filling the paladin's dead levels (it replaces nothing): starting at 7th level, and again at 8th, 11th, 13th, 14th, 16th, 17th and 19th level, the paladin gains a +1 bonus, each drawn from inspiring presence or discerning insight (%1 selections now).
Dead Levels (Righteous Cause)	KEY:ACF ~ Dead Levels (Righteous Cause) (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Paladin Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Paladin ACF Dead Levels (Righteous Cause)|(PaladinLVL>=7)+(PaladinLVL>=8)+(PaladinLVL>=11)+(PaladinLVL>=13)+(PaladinLVL>=14)+(PaladinLVL>=16)+(PaladinLVL>=17)+(PaladinLVL>=19)	SOURCEPAGE:p.416	DESC:Optional rule filling the paladin's dead levels (it replaces nothing): starting at 7th level, and again at 8th, 11th, 13th, 14th, 16th, 17th and 19th level, the paladin gains a +1 bonus, each drawn from inspiring presence or discerning insight (%1 selections now).|(PaladinLVL>=7)+(PaladinLVL>=8)+(PaladinLVL>=11)+(PaladinLVL>=13)+(PaladinLVL>=14)+(PaladinLVL>=16)+(PaladinLVL>=17)+(PaladinLVL>=19)
Dead Levels (Righteous Cause) (Inspiring Presence)	KEY:Paladin Dead Levels Righteous Cause ~ Inspiring Presence	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:PaladinACFDeadLevelsRighteousCause.SpecialQuality	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Leadership	SOURCEPAGE:p.416	DESC:The paladin becomes a rallying standard for decency and fairness: +1 to her Leadership score per selection, but only for the purpose of attracting 1st-level followers. Requires the Leadership feat.
Dead Levels (Righteous Cause) (Discerning Insight)	KEY:Paladin Dead Levels Righteous Cause ~ Discerning Insight	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:PaladinACFDeadLevelsRighteousCause.SpecialQuality	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	SOURCEPAGE:p.416	DESC:The paladin recognizes when a person is trustworthy: a +1 bonus per selection on Sense Motive checks to get a hunch about a subject's personality after a 1-minute conversation.
Detect Undead	KEY:Paladin ACF ~ Detect Undead (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PaladinACF.PaladinDetectEvil	PRECLASS:1,Paladin=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Detect Undead (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.418	DESC:Alternative class feature (paladin, 1st level). Lightbringer paladin: at will, a divination effect similar to detect evil that finds undead only (of any alignment), without concentration - at the moment she uses it she knows whether there are undead within a chosen 60-degree arc, their exact number and their exact locations. Spell-like, the equivalent of a 2nd-level spell. Replaces detect evil.
Detect Undead	KEY:ACF ~ Detect Undead (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Paladin Class Feature	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=ATWILL|CASTERLEVEL=PaladinLVL|Detect Undead	SOURCEPAGE:p.418	DESC:Lightbringer paladin: at will, a divination effect similar to detect evil that finds undead only (of any alignment), without concentration - at the moment she uses it she knows whether there are undead within a chosen 60-degree arc, their exact number and their exact locations. Spell-like, the equivalent of a 2nd-level spell. Replaces detect evil.
Domain Paladin	KEY:Paladin ACF ~ Domain Paladin (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PaladinACF.PaladinTurnUndead	PRECLASS:1,Paladin=3	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Domain Paladin (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.420	DESC:Alternative class feature (paladin, 3rd level). The paladin gives up her ability to turn undead and selects one paladin domain, which must belong to her deity (Chaos and Evil are banned; the listed domains are the usual ones). Paladin domains give no bonus spells, only a special ability based on the cleric domain.
Domain Paladin	KEY:ACF ~ Domain Paladin (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Paladin Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Paladin ACF Domain Paladin|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.420	DESC:The paladin gives up her ability to turn undead and selects one paladin domain, which must belong to her deity (Chaos and Evil are banned; the listed domains are the usual ones). Paladin domains give no bonus spells, only a special ability based on the cleric domain.
Domain Paladin (Death)	KEY:ACF ~ Domain Paladin (DMC) ~ Death	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:PaladinACFDomainPaladin.SpecialQuality	PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Death	SOURCEPAGE:p.420	DESC:Death ward as a standard action: you or a good-aligned creature you touch gains a bonus of +%1 (paladin level - 2) on all saves against death effects for 1 minute; %2 times per day (3 + Charisma modifier). Supernatural.|PaladinLVL-2|3+CHA
Domain Paladin (Knowledge)	KEY:ACF ~ Domain Paladin (DMC) ~ Knowledge	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:PaladinACFDomainPaladin.SpecialQuality	PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Knowledge	SOURCEPAGE:p.420	DESC:Divine inspiration: a check that functions exactly as bardic knowledge (supernatural), with a bonus of +%1 (paladin level + Charisma modifier), %2 times per day (1 + Charisma modifier).|PaladinLVL+CHA|1+CHA
Domain Paladin (Luck)	KEY:ACF ~ Domain Paladin (DMC) ~ Luck	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:PaladinACFDomainPaladin.SpecialQuality	PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Luck	SOURCEPAGE:p.420	DESC:Once per day (extraordinary), you may reroll one roll you have just made, before the DM declares the result; you must take the second roll.
Domain Paladin (Magic)	KEY:ACF ~ Domain Paladin (DMC) ~ Magic	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:PaladinACFDomainPaladin.SpecialQuality	PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Magic	CSKILL:Knowledge (Arcana)|Spellcraft	SOURCEPAGE:p.420	DESC:You use scrolls, wands and other spell completion or spell trigger devices as a wizard of level %1 (half your paladin level; actual wizard levels stack). Knowledge (arcana) and Spellcraft are class skills for you.|floor(PaladinLVL/2)
Domain Paladin (Protection)	KEY:ACF ~ Domain Paladin (DMC) ~ Protection	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:PaladinACFDomainPaladin.SpecialQuality	PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Protection	SOURCEPAGE:p.420	DESC:Protective ward (supernatural, standard action, once per day): you or someone you touch gains a resistance bonus of +%1 (paladin level - 2) on the next saving throw; abjuration, duration 1 hour.|PaladinLVL-2
Domain Paladin (Strength)	KEY:ACF ~ Domain Paladin (DMC) ~ Strength	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:PaladinACFDomainPaladin.SpecialQuality	PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Strength	SOURCEPAGE:p.420	DESC:Feat of strength (supernatural, free action, once per day): an enhancement bonus of +%1 (paladin level - 2) to Strength for 1 round.|PaladinLVL-2
Domain Paladin (War)	KEY:ACF ~ Domain Paladin (DMC) ~ War	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:PaladinACFDomainPaladin.SpecialQuality	PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,War	SOURCEPAGE:p.420	DESC:True warrior (supernatural, free action, once per day): for 1 round you bypass the damage reduction of any evil-aligned creature; activate before rolling the attack.
Gaze of Truth	KEY:Paladin ACF ~ Gaze of Truth (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PaladinACF.PaladinDetectEvil	PRECLASS:1,Paladin=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Gaze of Truth (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.426	DESC:Alternative class feature (paladin, 1st level). For you, justice is paramount: you can discern when someone is lying to you, as the spell discern lies, %1 times per day (1 + Charisma modifier, minimum 1), each use lasting 1 round per paladin level; the target gets a Will save (DC %2 = 10 + half your paladin level + Charisma modifier) - on a success you cannot discern lies from him for 24 hours. Detect evil is added to your paladin spell list. Replaces detect evil. (Discuss with your DM first: ready truth-finding can spoil a game of lies and intrigue.)
Gaze of Truth	KEY:ACF ~ Gaze of Truth (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Paladin Class Feature	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=max(1,1+CHA)|CASTERLEVEL=PaladinLVL|Discern Lies	SPELLLEVEL:CLASS|Paladin=1|Detect Evil	SOURCEPAGE:p.426	DESC:For you, justice is paramount: you can discern when someone is lying to you, as the spell discern lies, %1 times per day (1 + Charisma modifier, minimum 1), each use lasting 1 round per paladin level; the target gets a Will save (DC %2 = 10 + half your paladin level + Charisma modifier) - on a success you cannot discern lies from him for 24 hours. Detect evil is added to your paladin spell list. Replaces detect evil. (Discuss with your DM first: ready truth-finding can spoil a game of lies and intrigue.)|max(1,1+CHA)|10+floor(PaladinLVL/2)+CHA
Gnome Paladin	KEY:Paladin ACF ~ Gnome Paladin (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PaladinACF.PaladinGnome	PRECLASS:1,Paladin=1	PRERACE:1,Gnome%	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Gnome Paladin (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.426	DESC:Alternative class feature (paladin, 1st level). Changes emphasizing a gnome paladin's racial characteristics: Perform (comedy) replaces Knowledge (nobility and royalty) as a class skill (the removal is not enforced), and at 5th level she may summon a dire badger as her special mount, gaining special abilities at the same rate as a standard mount; other gnome paladin mounts include the black bear, boar, dire eagle, dire toad, dire weasel and wolverine (dire eagle and dire toad are not in the core data).
Gnome Paladin	KEY:ACF ~ Gnome Paladin (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Paladin Class Feature	CSKILL:Perform (Comedy)	COMPANIONLIST:Special Mount|Dire Animal (Dire Badger),Bear (Black),Boar,Dire Animal (Dire Weasel),Wolverine	SOURCEPAGE:p.426	DESC:Changes emphasizing a gnome paladin's racial characteristics: Perform (comedy) replaces Knowledge (nobility and royalty) as a class skill (the removal is not enforced), and at 5th level she may summon a dire badger as her special mount, gaining special abilities at the same rate as a standard mount; other gnome paladin mounts include the black bear, boar, dire eagle, dire toad, dire weasel and wolverine (dire eagle and dire toad are not in the core data).
Golarion Paladin	KEY:Paladin ACF ~ Golarion Paladin (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PaladinACF.PaladinRemoveDisease	PRECLASS:1,Paladin=6	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Golarion Paladin (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.426	DESC:Alternative class feature (paladin, 6th level). Light of Purity (Su): trained in the Holy Citadel of Light, %1 times per week (once at 6th level, one more per three levels, 5 at 18th) the paladin emits a radiance of blinding light acting as a daylight spell for %2 rounds (1 per paladin level); any undead within 30 feet takes %3d6 points of damage per round (1d6 per two paladin levels), Fortitude DC %4 (10 + half her level + Charisma modifier) for half. Replaces remove disease and all its increases.
Golarion Paladin	KEY:ACF ~ Golarion Paladin (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Paladin Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.426	DESC:Light of Purity (Su): trained in the Holy Citadel of Light, %1 times per week (once at 6th level, one more per three levels, 5 at 18th) the paladin emits a radiance of blinding light acting as a daylight spell for %2 rounds (1 per paladin level); any undead within 30 feet takes %3d6 points of damage per round (1d6 per two paladin levels), Fortitude DC %4 (10 + half her level + Charisma modifier) for half. Replaces remove disease and all its increases.|1+min(4,floor((PaladinLVL-6)/3))|PaladinLVL|floor(PaladinLVL/2)|10+floor(PaladinLVL/2)+CHA
Hunter of Fiends	KEY:Paladin ACF ~ Hunter of Fiends (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PaladinACF.PaladinSmiteEvil	PRECLASS:1,Paladin=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Hunter of Fiends (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.431	DESC:Alternative class feature (paladin, 1st level). You actively seek out demons and devils to slay: you gain outsider (evil) as a favored enemy, as the ranger ability, with a bonus of +%1 (half your paladin level, minimum +1) on Bluff, Listen, Sense Motive, Spot and Survival checks and on weapon damage rolls against them; no further favored enemies at later levels. You gain Track as a bonus feat and Survival and Knowledge (the planes) as class skills. Replaces smite evil; you give up Knowledge (nobility and royalty) as a class skill (not enforced).
Hunter of Fiends	KEY:ACF ~ Hunter of Fiends (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Paladin Class Feature	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Track	CSKILL:Survival|Knowledge (The Planes)	SOURCEPAGE:p.431	DESC:You actively seek out demons and devils to slay: you gain outsider (evil) as a favored enemy, as the ranger ability, with a bonus of +%1 (half your paladin level, minimum +1) on Bluff, Listen, Sense Motive, Spot and Survival checks and on weapon damage rolls against them; no further favored enemies at later levels. You gain Track as a bonus feat and Survival and Knowledge (the planes) as class skills. Replaces smite evil; you give up Knowledge (nobility and royalty) as a class skill (not enforced).|max(1,floor(PaladinLVL/2))
Pelor's Blessing	KEY:Paladin ACF ~ Pelor's Blessing (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PaladinACF.PaladinDivineHealth	PRECLASS:1,Paladin=3	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Pelor's Blessing (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.439	DESC:Alternative class feature (paladin, 3rd level). Lightbringer paladin: when he uses smite evil against undead, he gains an additional +2 bonus on the attack roll and deals +%1 extra damage (1 per two paladin levels). Extraordinary. Replaces divine health.
Pelor's Blessing	KEY:ACF ~ Pelor's Blessing (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Paladin Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.439	DESC:Lightbringer paladin: when he uses smite evil against undead, he gains an additional +2 bonus on the attack roll and deals +%1 extra damage (1 per two paladin levels). Extraordinary. Replaces divine health.|floor(PaladinLVL/2)
Power of the Self	KEY:Paladin ACF ~ Power of the Self (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PaladinACF.PaladinDivineGrave.PaladinDivineHealth.PaladinSpecialMount	PRECLASS:1,Paladin=4	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Power of the Self (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.441	DESC:Alternative class feature (paladin, 4th level). Lost one paladin: without a moral guide, his personal skills matter more than divine gifts - at 4th level and every four levels thereafter (8th, 12th, 16th, 20th) he gains a fighter bonus feat, as if he had taken levels in fighter (%1 now). Replaces divine grace, divine health and the special mount (abilities already gained are lost on becoming a lost one).
Power of the Self	KEY:ACF ~ Power of the Self (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Paladin Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Paladin ACF Power of the Self Feat|floor(PaladinLVL/4)	SOURCEPAGE:p.441	DESC:Lost one paladin: without a moral guide, his personal skills matter more than divine gifts - at 4th level and every four levels thereafter (8th, 12th, 16th, 20th) he gains a fighter bonus feat, as if he had taken levels in fighter (%1 now). Replaces divine grace, divine health and the special mount (abilities already gained are lost on becoming a lost one).|floor(PaladinLVL/4)
Smiting Arrow	KEY:Paladin ACF ~ Smiting Arrow (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PaladinACF.PaladinProficiencies	PRECLASS:1,Paladin=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Smiting Arrow (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.445	DESC:Alternative class feature (paladin, 1st level). You belong to a sacred group of priests who specialize in ranged weapons: you can smite evil with a ranged attack up to 30 feet. Replaces proficiency with heavy armor and shields (you keep simple and martial weapons and light and medium armor).
Smiting Arrow	KEY:ACF ~ Smiting Arrow (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Paladin Class Feature	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=ArmorProfMedium|TYPE=WeaponProfMartial	SOURCEPAGE:p.445	DESC:You belong to a sacred group of priests who specialize in ranged weapons: you can smite evil with a ranged attack up to 30 feet. Replaces proficiency with heavy armor and shields (you keep simple and martial weapons and light and medium armor).
Special Mounts	KEY:Paladin ACF ~ Special Mounts (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PaladinACF.PaladinSpecialMountList	PRECLASS:1,Paladin=5	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Special Mounts (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.446	DESC:Alternative class feature (paladin, 5th level). The compendium's compilation of creatures eligible as special mounts, by minimum paladin level (the mount is treated as that much lower level): 5th - baazrag, camel, diprotodon, riding dog, hippocampus, kank, Medium monstrous spider, porpoise, riding bird, sea tiger, Medium shark, velociraptor, warcamel, heavy or light warhorse, warpony; 6th (-1) - celestial riding dog/warhorse/warpony, deinonychus, dire badger, dire bat, dire weasel, dire wolf, hippogriff, monitor lizard, Large monstrous spider, Large shark, unicorn; 7th (-2) - dire boar, dire wolverine, giant eagle, giant owl, guardian steed, pegasus, rhinoceros, sea cat, terror bird; 8th (-3) - dire lion, griffon; 9th (-4) - bloodstriker, megaraptor; 10th (-5) - allosaurus, ankylosaurus; 12th (-7) - mastodon, quetzalcoatlus, triceratops, tyrannosaurus. Small riders only: baazrag, riding dog, Medium spider, porpoise, Medium shark, velociraptor, warpony, dire badger, dire bat, dire weasel, monitor lizard; aquatic only: hippocampus, porpoise, sea tiger, sharks, sea cat. (Offered here: the creatures in the core data; it replaces nothing.)
